"u.help.sub" = "Short, honest answers about Unrot on iPhone.";
"u.help.show" = "Shows the answer";
"u.help.hide" = "Hides the answer";
"u.help.q0" = "Can Unrot be made impossible to delete?";
"u.help.a0" = "Not completely: no app can on a normal iPhone. Make Unrot hard to delete (You › Hard to delete) gets iPhone itself to refuse deleting apps until a date you choose. A guardian or a supervised iPhone is stronger.";
"u.help.q1" = "Why isn't my time given back growing?";
"u.help.a1" = "Choose your feed apps in Shield first. Unrot counts whole days, from the first full day after that, in ten-minute steps that Screen Time reports. Today joins tomorrow.";
"u.help.q2" = "What does Unrot see?";
"u.help.a2" = "Very little. iPhone never shows Unrot which sites you visit or what you watch. It keeps one number a day, how far your chosen apps got, plus what you write yourself. All of it stays on this iPhone.";
"u.help.q3" = "Why did my glass crack?";
"u.help.a3" = "Because you said you went looking for adult content and it was stopped. iPhone does not tell apps when a page is blocked, so only you can say so. Breathe within ten minutes and the crack is sealed with gold.";
"u.help.q4" = "Is adult content blocked everywhere?";
"u.help.a4" = "In layers: six Safari blockers with a signed list, Apple's adult filter for other browsers, and a DNS filter for every app. Turn all three on in Shield. No filter catches every page or image.";
"u.help.q5" = "Does a hard day reset my sprout?";
"u.help.a5" = "Never. Time given back and your garden are never wiped. A heavy day is a small plant; adult content getting through breaks the glass, and new glass goes in.";
"u.help.q6" = "When do I get my Screen Time passcode back?";
"u.help.a6" = "On the date you chose. Open Hard to delete then and Unrot shows it, after checking the date on Apple's clock too, so moving your iPhone's clock forward doesn't open it early.";
"u.help.q7" = "How do I turn Unrot off?";
"u.help.a7" = "Each layer turns off in Shield or in You › Everything else. While a commitment or lock runs, Unrot holds its own switches until the date; that is the point of it.";
